From d4996ba7f8f4378056607e0ce37367efdd3cf2c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:23:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 162/210] media: amlogic: add a video deinterlacer driver

The G12A, G12B, SM1 and S4 SoCs have a video deinterlacer (DI) that
runs from its own timing generators and writes its output to memory,
but there is no driver for it, so interlaced video cannot be
deinterlaced in hardware.

Add a V4L2 mem2mem driver. Each woven interlaced NV12 frame is processed
one field at a time: the pre stage writes a noise-reduced field and its
motion data to an internal buffer, and the post stage blends each field
with the fields either side using that motion, giving two progressive
NV12 frames per input frame. Outputs lag the input by one field, and the
first two fields of a stream are interpolated until the history fills.

S4 keeps the G12A processing blocks but moves the read and write memory
interfaces and the line generators to new register blocks, adds
top-level path and secure registers, and changes the layout of the pre
and post control registers. Describe the moved registers in per-layout
tables and branch on the remaining differences.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
